main.py,main.py,9fae32bd47df0d0a70a773cd95ea2f9127a7bbb7,Amir-Hossein-shamsi/Text-to-SQL,https://api.github.com/repositories/1007858143/contents/main.py?ref=19c36b7d6336a9fc467afd7f528f4b1b71fc2ed8,https://api.github.com/repositories/1007858143/git/blobs/9fae32bd47df0d0a70a773cd95ea2f9127a7bbb7,https://github.com/Amir-Hossein-shamsi/Text-to-SQL/blob/19c36b7d6336a9fc467afd7f528f4b1b71fc2ed8/main.py,"A powerful CLI tool that converts natural language questions into executable MySQL queries using LLMs and executes them on your database. Perfect for quick data exploration, prototyping, and demos!",,0,0,0,2,2025-06-24T16:38:24Z,1,0,"# Text-to-SQL 🚀

A powerful CLI tool that converts natural language questions into executable MySQL queries using LLMs (via [Ollama](https://ollama.com/)) and executes them on your database. Perfect for quick data exploration, prototyping, and demos!

---

## ✨ Features

- **Natural Language to SQL**: Ask questions in plain English, get SQL queries.
- **LLM-Powered**: Uses your favorite Ollama model (configurable).
- **MySQL Support**: Connects to any MySQL-compatible database.
- **Schema-Aware**: LLM sees your schema for accurate queries.
- **Easy Data Bootstrapping**: Instantly create tables and fill with dummy data.
- **Docker-Ready**: Includes a ready-to-use MySQL Docker setup.

---

## 🏗️ Project Structure

```
.
├── main.py            # Main CLI logic
├── db_utils.py        # DB schema creation & dummy data
├── .env               # Environment variables (model, DB URI, etc.)
├── docker-compose.yml # MySQL Docker setup
└── result.txt         # Query results output
```

---

## ⚡ Quickstart

### 1. Clone & Install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Amir-Hossein-shamsi/Text-to-SQL.git
cd textToSql
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 2. Configure Environment

Edit `.env` as needed:

```properties
OLLAMA_MODEL=deepseek-r1:7b
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
DATABASE_URI=mysql+pymysql://myuser:mypassword@localhost:3306/mydatabase
```

### 3. Start MySQL with Docker (optional)

```bash
docker-compose up -d
```

### 4. Bootstrap Database (tables + dummy data)

```bash
python main.py --init-db --num-rows 1000 --question ""How many employees are there?""
```

### 5. Ask Questions!

```bash
python main.py --question ""List all employees in the Sales department.""
```

Results are saved to `result.txt`.

---

## 🛠️ CLI Usage

| Argument         | Description                                            | Example                   |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------- |
| `--question, -q` | Natural language question (required)                   | `""Show all HR employees""` |
| `--init-db`      | Create tables and insert dummy data before running     | (flag, no value)          |
| `--num-rows`     | Number of dummy employees to insert (with `--init-db`) | `--num-rows 500`          |

---

## 🧩 Example

```bash
python main.py --init-db --num-rows 200 --question ""How many employees are in Engineering?""
```

---

## 📝 Notes

- **Ollama** must be running and accessible at the URL in `.env`.
- The tool only supports MySQL (or compatible) databases.
- Results are written to `result.txt` in the project directory.

---

## 🧑‍💻 Authors

- [AmirHossein Shamsi](https://github.com/Amir-Hossein-shamsi)

