ingest.py,ingest.py,f8ddc0e7305379c2a215ff1fdc9569109f2ec3c5,yaaashhh725/Local_rag_app,https://api.github.com/repositories/1044084740/contents/ingest.py?ref=1d5cc71432c1805da325bdca303d49b87d831241,https://api.github.com/repositories/1044084740/git/blobs/f8ddc0e7305379c2a215ff1fdc9569109f2ec3c5,https://github.com/yaaashhh725/Local_rag_app/blob/1d5cc71432c1805da325bdca303d49b87d831241/ingest.py,A retrieval augmented generation application that runs completely on your machine.,,0,0,0,1,2025-08-25T06:55:43Z,0,0,"# PDF Q&A with Evidence Highlighting Completely Locally

This project is a Streamlit-based application for question answering over PDF documents. It uses LangChain, HuggingFace embeddings, and Ollama LLMs to retrieve relevant information from uploaded PDFs and highlights the evidence directly on the document pages.

## Features
- Upload PDF documents
- Hybrid text extraction (native and OCR)
- Chunking and vector storage with ChromaDB
- Question answering using LLMs
- Source highlighting with bounding boxes

## Setup
1. Clone this repository.
2. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```
3. (Optional) Install and run Ollama for LLM support: [Ollama Installation Guide](https://ollama.com/download)
4. Start the app:
   ```bash
   streamlit run app.py
   ```

## Usage
- Upload a PDF using the sidebar.
- Ask questions about the document.
- View answers and highlighted sources.

## Screenshot
[![App Screenshot](image/image.png)](image/image.png~)
<!-- Replace LINK_TO_SCREENSHOT with your actual screenshot URL -->

## File Structure
- `app.py` - Streamlit UI and main app logic
- `ingest.py` - PDF ingestion and vector store creation
- `qa.py` - Question answering system
- `config.py` - Configuration settings
- `requirements.txt` - Python dependencies
- `documents/` - Folder for source PDFs
- `vector_store/` - Persistent vector store
- `temp_uploads/` and `temp_vector_store/` - Temporary files and stores

