## Summary
This repo showcases a simple, yet effective tool for document summarization. It can work with plain-text and PDF documents in any language supported by the underlying LLM (Mistral by default).

![Summarization Process](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400?text=Summarization+Process)

## Setup

### Installing Dependencies

Install the following dependencies (on macOS):

- Python 3 installation (e.g. [Miniconda](https://docs.conda.io/projects/miniconda/en/latest/) or [Homebrew package](https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/python@3.10))
- Python packages: run `pip3 install -r requirements.txt`
- Download `mistral-7b-openorca.Q5_K_M.gguf` model from Hugging Face [TheBloke/Mistral-7B-OpenOrca-GGUF](https://huggingface.co/TheBloke/Mistral-7B-OpenOrca-GGUF/tree/main) repo into the local `models` directory.

![Installation Steps](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400?text=Installation+Steps)

Note: You can experiment with alternative models by updating the `MODEL_FILE` and `MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW` variables in `web-ui.py` and/or `Notebook.ipynb`.

## Running

### Web UI

To run the Web UI, execute:
```sh
python3 ./web-ui.py
```
This should open the Web UI interface in the browser.

![Web UI](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400?text=Web+UI)

### Jupyter Notebook

The tool can be used in Jupyter Labs/Notebook as well. Open `Notebook.ipynb` in [Jupyter Labs](https://jupyterlab.readthedocs.io/en/stable/getting_started/installation.html#conda).

## Details

### Workflow

Depending on the document size, this tool works in the following modes:
1. If the whole document fits into the model's context window, summarization is performed by adding a relevant summarization prompt.
2. For large documents, a ""map-reduce"" pattern is applied:
   - The document is first split into smaller chunks using `RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter`, which tries to respect paragraph and sentence boundaries.
   - Each chunk is summarized separately (map step).
   - Chunk summaries are summarized again to produce the final summary (reduce step).

![Workflow](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400?text=Workflow)

### Local Processing
All processing is done locally on the user's machine.
- The quantized Mistral model (`mistral-7b-openorca.Q5_K_M.gguf`) is approximately 5.1 GB.

### Performance

Relatively small to medium documents (a few pages) should fit into a single context window, resulting in a processing time of around 40 seconds on an Apple MBP with an M1 chip.

![Performance](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400?text=Performance)

## Troubleshooting

No known issues.
